# Verible lint rules for the parser RTL (Phase 5/6).
#
# We run verible-verilog-lint as a second, independent SystemVerilog linter
# alongside Verilator -Wall (nix run .#parser-analyze). The two deviations below
# adopt traditional hardware-RTL conventions over verible's Google-style
# defaults; every other rule stays enabled and must pass.
#
#   parameter-name-style : accept ALL_CAPS constants (the long-standing Verilog
#                          convention for parameters/localparams — e.g. PKT_MAX,
#                          CAM_DEPTH — as well as CamelCase).
#   unpacked-dimensions-range-ordering : allow explicit [0:N-1] memory ranges,
#                          which state the address range outright.
parameter-name-style=localparam_style:CamelCase|ALL_CAPS;parameter_style:CamelCase|ALL_CAPS
-unpacked-dimensions-range-ordering
